# Rule Management Workflow

## Purpose
Define a deterministic workflow for adding, editing, and syncing rules.

## Trigger
Apply when user asks to create, update, move, reorganize, or sync rules.

## Source of Truth
- Keryx's own shipped rules: `src/gdskills/bundled/rules/core/*.mdc` in the
  keryx repository — installed into `.metaproject/rules/core/*.mdc` by `keryx
  init`/`keryx update` (the installed copy is regenerated wholesale on every
  run; edit the source, not the installed copy). There is no `keryx install`
  command.
- A project's own instructions: the project's root `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md`.
  Edit those files directly, then run `keryx rules sync` (or `keryx rules
  distill` for a large entrypoint) to import them into
  `.metaproject/rules/<name>.md` (e.g. `agents-md.md`, `claude-md.md`) and
  refresh the routing index. A project-owned rule never lives under
  `.metaproject/rules/core/` — that tree mirrors only keryx's own shipped
  rules and is overwritten wholesale by `keryx init`/`keryx update`.
- Root always-on file: `AGENTS.md`

## Mandatory Clarification Step
Before creating or editing any rule, the agent MUST ask and confirm:
1. Target location
2. Target folder name
3. Rule file name (semantic, no numeric prefix)
4. Rule scope and trigger conditions

## Mandatory Behavior
1. Update or create keryx's shipped thematic rule files only under
   `src/gdskills/bundled/rules/core/` (installed to `.metaproject/rules/core/`).
   A project's own instructions belong in its root `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md`,
   imported via `keryx rules sync`/`keryx rules distill`.
2. Keep all rule files in English.
3. Keep frontmatter valid YAML.
4. If core files changed, keep `AGENTS.md` consistent and re-run synchronization.
5. Run synchronization only after source files are updated.

## How to Run Synchronization
After editing rules under `src/gdskills/bundled/rules/`, run `keryx update`
(or `keryx init` on a fresh project) to regenerate the installed copy at
`.metaproject/rules/`. This stays inside the project — it never writes to a
home-directory (`~`) location.

After editing the project's own root `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md`, run:

```bash
keryx rules sync
```

This imports the root `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` into `.metaproject/rules/` and
refreshes the routing index. It is also project-local and writes no
home-directory (`~`) path.

## Rule File Standard
Every core rule MUST include:
- Purpose
- When To Apply
- Mandatory Behavior
- Output Contract (when the rule defines user-facing deliverables)
- Optional examples

## Output Contract for Rule Work
- Any produced rule text must be Markdown.
- Any code example must be fenced.
- Final response language must follow user query language.

## Apply Changes Workflow
After rule changes, ask whether to apply changes.
If approved: create branch from `main`, commit, and open PR to `main`.
